<img width="350" height="525" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-Apple-Slaw-350x525.jpg" class="webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image" alt="Kale Apple Slaw in a bowl with two tablespoons on the side." style="display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear:both;max-width: 100%;" link_thumbnail="" decoding="async" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-Apple-Slaw-350x525.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-Apple-Slaw-400x600.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-Apple-Slaw-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-Apple-Slaw-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-Apple-Slaw-150x225.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-Apple-Slaw.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" />
<div class="wp-block-group is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained">
<p>Using apples in a savory salad isn&rsquo;t new, but I think most apple salads miss a chance to pair them with something as sturdy and earthy as kale. A good dressing is key, especially when kale is involved, because let&rsquo;s be honest, on its own, it&rsquo;s not everyone&rsquo;s favorite (my husband would agree).&nbsp;</p>



<p>For me, the magic is in the balance of textures and tastes. Sweet, crisp apples meet earthy kale, all tied together with a dreamy maple Dijon dressing. Then comes the crunch from sunflower seeds, which makes every bite a little more exciting.</p>



<p>I call it a slaw because I was inspired by the Kale Apple Slaw at Tropical Smoothie Caf&eacute;, a cult-favorite dish that I loved so much that I had to recreate it in my own kitchen. It&rsquo;s the kind of salad I make as part of my weekly meal prep because it holds up so well in the fridge.&nbsp;</p>



<p>One bite and I think you&rsquo;ll agree, let&rsquo;s make it together.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-kale-and-apple-slaw-ingredients-nbsp">Kale and Apple Slaw Ingredients&nbsp;</h2>



<p>You only need a handful of produce and a few basic pantry staples to make this fresh kale apple coleslaw. You&rsquo;ll find the full list in the recipe card below, but here are a few helpful notes from my testing on ingredients and substitutions:</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-large"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-apple-coleslaw-Ingredients-1200x800.jpg" alt="Ingredients for the recipe from the top view." class="wp-image-83424" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-apple-coleslaw-Ingredients.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-apple-coleslaw-Ingredients-350x233.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-apple-coleslaw-Ingredients-768x512.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-apple-coleslaw-Ingredients-400x267.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-apple-coleslaw-Ingredients-150x100.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-apple-coleslaw-Ingredients.jpg"></figure>



<p><strong>For the Dressing</strong></p>



<p>It is no secret that the dressing is the most important part of any kale salad, as sturdy kale leaves can use a ton of help when it comes to flavoring. I decided to use my <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/maple-dijon-dressing/">Maple Dijon Vinaigrette</a> as it offers the perfect balance of sweet and tangy flavors that complements the rest of the ingredients.</p>



<p><strong>Below are a couple of notes from my recipe testing:</strong></p>



<p><strong>Maple syrup:</strong> I love the caramel-like sweetness it brings with the Dijon. For a lighter, citrusy twist, swap it with orange juice. Honey also works if you prefer a richer sweetness. I tested this slaw with all three, and while each works, they give the salad a slightly different character.</p>



<p><strong>Apple cider vinegar:</strong> A key ingredient. It adds acidity to the dressing and also ties the apples into the overall flavor. If you don&rsquo;t have it, red wine vinegar works too, but the taste is a little sharper.</p>



<p><strong>For The Slaw</strong></p>



<p><strong>Apple:</strong> Crisp, firm apples hold up best. Fuji, Pink Lady, and Honeycrisp are my top picks, though tart Granny Smith is also great. Whatever you choose, slice or cube them just before serving to avoid browning.</p>



<p><strong>Kale:</strong> I usually go with curly kale, but lacinato kale (aka Tuscan kale) works just as well. Each type has a different flavor and texture. If you&rsquo;re not sure which to use, my <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/types-of-kale/">Types of Kale</a> guide can help you decide.</p>



<p><strong>Seeds and nuts:</strong> I often use sunflower seeds, especially when I want to keep the recipe nut-free. When I do use nuts, I prefer raw almonds, pecans, or walnuts. Their mild taste lets the kale and apples stand out.</p>



<p><strong>Cabbage:</strong> Red cabbage adds color and a subtle earthy note, but green cabbage works if that&rsquo;s what you have. The thinner you slice it, the better it absorbs the dressing. I usually shred it with this insert I keep in my food processor, which I&rsquo;ve found safer and quicker than a traditional mandoline. If you&rsquo;re pressed for time, a bagged coleslaw mix is a fine shortcut.</p>



<p><strong>Red Onion:</strong> Even though red onion has a stronger taste, I like using it here because it stands up well against hearty kale and crisp cabbage. If you prefer something milder, green onions are a good alternative.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-how-to-make-kale-apple-slaw">How to Make Kale Apple Slaw</h2>



<p>One of my favorite things about this kale apple salad, besides how fresh and crunchy it is, is how easily it fits into any meal. It lasts for days in the fridge and pairs with just about anything. Here&rsquo;s how I put it together:</p>



<p><strong>Step 1 &ndash; Make the salad dressing:</strong> In a small bowl, whisk together the maple syrup, dijon mustard, apple cider vinegar, olive oil, salt, and pepper.&nbsp;</p>



<p>Then, add the sliced red onion to the dressing mixture and let it steep in the mixture while you prepare the rest of the ingredients. The vinegar takes away the sharp edge of raw onion, making it softer and slightly sweeter.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="744" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Maple-Mustard-Cider-Dressing.jpg" alt="person showing how to make maple dijon vinaigrette" class="wp-image-49040" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Maple-Mustard-Cider-Dressing.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Maple-Mustard-Cider-Dressing-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Maple-Mustard-Cider-Dressing-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Maple-Mustard-Cider-Dressing-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Maple-Mustard-Cider-Dressing-150x93.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Maple-Mustard-Cider-Dressing.jpg"></figure>



<p><strong>Step 2 &ndash; Prepare the salad:</strong> In a large mixing bowl, add the shredded kale, shredded carrots, and sliced red cabbage. Drizzle with the dressing and red onion, then use your hands to lightly massage the kale to break down the tougher parts of the leaves, making them more tender, less bitter, and better at soaking up the dressing.&nbsp;</p>


<div class="su-note" style="border-color:#d9d8d7;border-radius:1px;-moz-border-radius:1px;-webkit-border-radius:1px;"><div class="su-note-inner su-u-clearfix su-u-trim" style="background-color:#f3f2f1;border-color:#ffffff;color:#000;border-radius:1px;-moz-border-radius:1px;-webkit-border-radius:1px;">



<p><strong>Pro Tip:</strong> <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/how-to-massage-kale/">Massaging kale</a> might seem like an unusual practice, but I believe it is the secret to making kale tender, which is a common complaint among many people. Once massaged, it transforms into something much softer and easier to enjoy.</p>


</div></div>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1499" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/How-to-make-kale-and-apple-slaw.jpg" alt="Person showing how to make kale apple slaw with step by step photos." class="wp-image-49042" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/How-to-make-kale-and-apple-slaw.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/How-to-make-kale-and-apple-slaw-400x500.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/How-to-make-kale-and-apple-slaw-350x437.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/How-to-make-kale-and-apple-slaw-768x959.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/How-to-make-kale-and-apple-slaw-150x187.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/How-to-make-kale-and-apple-slaw.jpg"></figure>



<p><strong>Step 3 &ndash; Serve:</strong> Top it off with the sliced apple and sunflower seeds. Toss the mixture one more time to evenly distribute the toppings, and serve immediately for the best crunch and freshest flavor.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="744" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-apple-salad.jpg" alt="Tropical smoothie kale apple slaw recipe in a bowl. " class="wp-image-49043" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-apple-salad.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-apple-salad-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-apple-salad-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-apple-salad-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-apple-salad-150x93.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-apple-salad.jpg"></figure>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-how-to-make-ahead-and-store">How To Make Ahead and Store?</h2>



<p>This easy slaw recipe is meal-prep friendly, holding up beautifully in the fridge for days, so you can enjoy a crisp side dish all week long. Here are the best ways to ensure it stays fresh:</p>



<p><strong>Make ahead:</strong> The Maple Dijon Vinaigrette can be prepared up to 2 days in advance and stored in a mason jar in the fridge. On the day you plan to serve, simply toss it with the kale, cabbage, and carrots, then add the apples just before serving. Assembly takes only about 5 minutes.</p>



<p><strong>Storage:</strong> Once assembled, the slaw will keep in an airtight container in the fridge for up to 3 days. For the best texture and color, slice the apples right before eating to prevent browning.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1800" data-pin-description="Kale Apple Slaw like you find at Tropical Smoothie Cafe made in 15 minutes! Vegan &amp; gluten-free, it&rsquo;s perfect by itself or to serve with tacos and meat dishes." data-pin-title="Kale Apple Slaw" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-and-Apple-Slaw.jpg" alt="Kale and Apple Slaw in a bowl with two spoons on the side" class="wp-image-49037" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-and-Apple-Slaw.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-and-Apple-Slaw-400x600.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-and-Apple-Slaw-350x525.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-and-Apple-Slaw-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-and-Apple-Slaw-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-and-Apple-Slaw-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Kale-and-Apple-Slaw.jpg"></figure>
